# scripts/release/check-path.sh exercises the release path on a copy of
# the tree (#609): the edits of prepare.sh with the next version, the move
# of [Unreleased] and the fragments with its count (one entry, a fragment, and
# the check's own dummy fragment), the notes of the GitHub
# Release with absolute links, the links of the moved changelog, and the
# version of the tree pinned outside comments, here in a FileCheck pattern
# and in code, which it reports until they match any version.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/release_path.py %S/../.. | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: release path: 1.4.0 -> 1.5.0, 3 entries moved, 3 in [1.5.0]
# CHECK-NEXT: release path: notes, {{[0-9]+}} lines, 0 bad link(s)
# CHECK-NEXT: 0 broken link(s)
# CHECK-NEXT: release path: 2 use(s) of 1.4.0 outside comments
# CHECK-DAG: the previous version 1.4.0: lib/Version.cpp:2: const char *v = "1.4.0";
# CHECK-DAG: the previous version 1.4.0: test/Driver/version.test:3: # CHECK: MDIR 1.4.0
# CHECK: release path: FAILED
# CHECK-NOT: test/Driver/version.test:2
# CHECK: -- after the fix --
# CHECK: release path: 0 use(s) of 1.4.0 outside comments
# CHECK-NEXT: release path: ok
# CHECK: status 1 then 0
